{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_ota", "label": "OTA.md \u2014 live web updates", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_ota_live_web_updates", "label": "Live web updates (OTA web-bundle swap, v0.1.11)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L1-L4; L32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frontend, styling and logic changes reach the phones at the next launch without a new APK / IPA; nothing goes to Capgo (manual mode, empty updateUrl / statsUrl / channelUrl)."}, {"id": "docs_ota_capacitor_updater_plugin", "label": "@capgo/capacitor-updater plugin (CapacitorUpdater, manual mode)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L32; L45-L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_ota_app_updates_bucket", "label": "app-updates Storage bucket (<channel>/<version>.zip + manifest.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L9; L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public bucket; a bundle is ~10 MB (OCR data dominates) against a 50 MB limit; old bundles stay."}, {"id": "docs_ota_update_check_flow", "label": "Update check (4 s after launch, on resume \u2264 every 30 min, or manual)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L10-L15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads the manifest \u2192 parseManifest() \u2192 decide() \u2192 download() with the SHA-256 \u2192 next(); the banner offers \u00ab\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b \u0627\u0644\u0622\u0646\u00bb and \u2715 applies it silently at the next cold start, so nobody has to open Settings. The flow diagram still says an 8 s manifest timeout while LIMITS.manifest and the v0.1.12 section say 10 s."}, {"id": "docs_ota_update_rules", "label": "OTA install rules (well-formed manifest inside our bucket, newer build only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L17-L24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The manifest URL must be a .zip inside our app-updates bucket and manifest.build must exceed the running bundle's __BUILD__.ts."}, {"id": "docs_ota_native_line", "label": "Native line (ota.config.json \u2192 nativeLine)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L19-L23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bundle installs only if its nativeLine equals the shell's (versionName <nativeLine>.<build>); bump it for any change that needs a new shell, and older shells then ignore new bundles. Line 1 = first shells (v0.1.11); line 2 = v0.27.0 camera work."}, {"id": "docs_ota_bundle_integrity", "label": "Bundle integrity (SHA-256 verified download)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L25-L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plugin refuses a hash mismatch and the publish script re-checks that the public URL serves exactly the hashed bytes; manifest signing is not enabled \u2014 HTTPS + our bucket + the hash are the chain for now."}, {"id": "docs_ota_rollback", "label": "Unhealthy bundle rollback (notifyAppReady, engspace.ota.bad)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L27-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app confirms a bundle only if the root rendered with no uncaught error and no error screen; otherwise the plugin reverts within 15 s and the failed version is never downloaded again."}, {"id": "docs_ota_new_shell_wins", "label": "New shell wins (native build number raised on every release)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L30-L31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plugin drops a downloaded bundle when a newer shell is installed over it, so a fresh APK is never stuck on an old bundle."}, {"id": "docs_ota_time_limits", "label": "Nothing waits forever \u2014 updater time limits (v0.1.12)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L34-L42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plugin's download() had no deadline and its worker retried forever; now manifest 10 s, plugin calls 6 s, download watchdog 30 s idle / 3 min, whole check 200 s; a running check is joined and a manual check always ends in a message."}, {"id": "docs_ota_plugin_proxy_pitfall", "label": "Never await a Capacitor plugin object (Proxy then pitfall, v0.1.13)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L44-L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A plugin Proxy answers then with a native wrapper, so a promise resolved with it never settles \u2014 the real cause of the endless spinner; promises carry the module and the plugin is read from it synchronously."}, {"id": "docs_ota_publish_web_update", "label": "Publish web update (workflow + scripts/ota/publish.mjs)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L8-L9; L41-L42; L52-L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "check \u2192 build with the live keys \u2192 zip dist/ \u2192 upload to <channel>; SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN reads the service key at run time (masked); the workflow fails unless the manifest is public and CORS allows the WebView origins."}, {"id": "docs_ota_broadcast_app_update", "label": "Update notice broadcast (broadcast_app_update(), v0.1.14)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L59-L67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Service role only: one update notice (category system) per member with the phone app registered and not suspended \u2014 once per bundle, so a re-run sends nothing twice; older shells just open the app and the launch / resume check shows the banner."}, {"id": "docs_ota_store_policy", "label": "What OTA cannot do + store policy (Google Play, Apple 3.3.2 / 2.5.2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L69-L72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything native (plugins, permissions, push config, zoom lock, icons / splash) needs a new APK / IPA and a nativeLine bump; web-content updates are allowed while the app keeps its purpose."}, {"id": "docs_ota_settings_panel", "label": "Settings \u2192 \u0627\u0644\u062a\u062d\u062f\u064a\u062b\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0641\u0648\u0631\u064a\u0629 (active bundle, status, manual check)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L15; L29; L40; L50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shows built-in vs downloaded bundle, download %, rollbacks and \u00abshell <version> \u00b7 updater linked|missing\u00bb."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_ota", "target": "docs_ota_live_web_updates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L1-L4; L32", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_ota", "target": "docs_ota_capacitor_updater_plugin", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/OTA.md", "source_location": "L32; L45-L50", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_ota", "target": "docs_ota_app_updates